DECISIONS 305, 320, decision 213: go embedded mode is not built yet (owed for v0.2), so stage E refuses the
emit with E8019 `unbuilt` at its mode, naming baked mode instead, and judges it by no rule of its mode:
a variant-level export fn (VariantMethod) draws nothing more.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A reward.
variant Reward {
  /// Some gold.
  gold {
    /// How much.
    amount: Int
  }
  /// Nothing.
  nothing

  /// What it is worth.
  export fn worth(self) -> Int {
    return match self {
      gold(g) => g.amount
      nothing => 0
    }
  }

  check worth() >= 0 else "negative"
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", mode: embedded }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:24:51
  emit go cannot use embedded mode yet; use baked mode

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
